### UniBite — Test: POST /api/requests/approve  +  /api/requests/reject
### Run #1 first; the HTTP Client keeps the session cookie for the rest.
###
### PREP: you need pending requests in the DB. In phpMyAdmin (db unibite, SQL),
### insert two, using one of YOUR active listings and another user as consumer:
###   INSERT INTO requests (listing_id, consumer_id, slot, status)
###   VALUES (2, 3, 1, 'pending'), (2, 3, 2, 'pending');
### Then check their ids in the `requests` table and put them below.

### 1) Login
POST http://localhost/unibite/api/auth/login.php
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "dimitris",
  "password": "unibite2025"
}

### 2) Approve request #1 (expect success; listing's portions_available drops by 1)
POST http://localhost/unibite/api/requests/approve.php
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

request_id=1

### 3) Reject request #2 (expect success + refunded:true; consumer gets +1 point)
POST http://localhost/unibite/api/requests/reject.php
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

request_id=2

### 4) Approve #1 again (expect 409 Request is not pending)
POST http://localhost/unibite/api/requests/approve.php
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

request_id=1

### 5) Approve a non-existent request (expect 404 Request not found)
POST http://localhost/unibite/api/requests/approve.php
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

request_id=99999
